index 28b0891..1bf97db 100644
--- a/saas/README.md
+++ b/saas/README.md
@@ -46,6 +46,31 @@ This will ask for your 1password authorization to read and set the environment v
 * [Staging](https://dashboard.stripe.com/acct_1SdTbuRvb8txnPBR/test/dashboard)
 * [Production](https://dashboard.stripe.com/acct_1SNy97RwChFE4it8/dashboard)
 
+## Billing
+
+Hosted Fizzy has three plans:
+
+| Plan | Price | Cards | Storage |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Free | - | 1,000 | 1 GB |
+| Unlimited | $20/month | Unlimited | 5 GB |
+| Unlimited+ | $25/month | Unlimited | 500 GB |
+
+Stripe hosts checkout and the customer portal. Subscription changes arrive
+via webhooks posted to `/stripe/webhooks`, which sync `Account::Subscription`
+and, with it, the account's plan. Free accounts that run out of cards can
+keep drafting, but publishing and API creation are refused until they
+upgrade (or support comps them or overrides their limits from
+`/admin/accounts`).
+
+The integration reads these environment variables:
+
+* `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` — API key used to create checkout and portal sessions.
+* `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET` — verifies webhook signatures; when unset
+  (development, tests) payloads are trusted as posted.
+* `STRIPE_PRICE_ID_UNLIMITED`, `STRIPE_PRICE_ID_UNLIMITED_PLUS` — the price
+  ids checkout sessions are created with and webhooks are matched against.
+
 ## Working with Push Notifications
 
 To test native push notifications (APNs and FCM) locally, start the dev server with the `--push` flag:
